      "data": {
        "text": "**Selecting Text-to-Speech**\n\nI've decided on Google Cloud Text-to-Speech for text synthesis. Next, I'll integrate the necessary provider-specific code into `synthesize_text.py` to create the audio byte stream. This means focusing on the API calls for Google's service within the file.\n\n\n**Implementing Google TTS**\n\nI've made progress on `synthesize_text.py`. The initial decision to use Google Cloud Text-to-Speech is firm. I am now focused on integrating the necessary API calls. The plan is to initialize a `client` and call `synthesize_speech` within the Python file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861870549,
          "start": 1789861867514
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc14affa001bufV1sSN9qbEMV",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc14aabc0015twb0cHerA5eim",
      "session_id": "ses_f43eb55c6ffeSqISKyzc3RLQWa",
      "time_created": 1789861867514,
      "time_updated": 1789861870550
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "aaynkn8woHelQSaH",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nfrom google.cloud import texttospeech\n\ndef synthesize_text_to_audio(text, output_filename=\"output.mp3\"):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\n\n    Args:\n        text (str): The plain text to synthesize.\n        output_filename (str): The name of the file to save the audio to.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Instantiates a client\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    # Set the text input to be synthesized\n    synthesis_input = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(text=text)\n\n    # Build the voice request, select the language code (\"en-US\") and the ssml\n    # voice gender (\"neutral\")\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\", ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL\n    )\n\n    # Select the type of audio file you want returned\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    # Perform the text-to-speech request on the text input with the selected\n    # voice parameters and audio file type\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        input=synthesis_input, voice=voice, audio_config=audio_config\n    )\n\n    # The response's audio_content is binary.\n    with open(output_filename, \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(response.audio_content)\n        print(f'Audio content written to file \"{output_filename}\"')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Set the GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS environment variable to your\n    # service account key file path before running this script.\n    # For example:\n    # export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=\"/path/to/your/keyfile.json\"\n    text_to_synthesize = \"Hello, this is a test of Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\"\n    synthesize_text_to_audio(text_to_synthesize, \"hello_world.mp3\")\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_text.py"
          },
